<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kutrigurs</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kutrigurs were a Turkic nomadic people of the Pontic steppe west of the Don in the 6th century, closely related to the Utigurs to the east. They raided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a> repeatedly, and in 559 their leader Zabergan reached the walls of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> before being driven off by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a>. Justinian then set the Utigurs against them, and both peoples were weakened before being absorbed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a>.</p></div>
